    "title": "Eaton Rapids police located man missing since July 6 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ken Palmer ,\n13 hours ago UPDATED 1:40 p.m. July 8: Cass Keenan has been located and is safe, Eaton Rapids police said.\nOriginal story:\nEATON RAPIDS — Police are looking for information about a man who has been missing since early Monday, July 6.\nCass Keenan, 31, was last seen about 1 a.m. Monday, Eaton Rapids police said in a Facebook post.\nKeenan was described as about 6-foot-4. He has ties to the Eaton Rapids, St Johns and Lansing areas.\nWhen last seen, he was wearing khaki pants and a black short-sleeve shirt, and he was driving a gray Ford F-150 pickup truck with the plate number of B0L04ME.\nAnyone with information is asked to call 911 or Detective Ken Snyder at (517) 507-3534.\nContact Ken Palmer at kpalmer@lsj.com . Follow him on X @KBPalm_lsj .\nThis article originally appeared on Lansing State Journal: Eaton Rapids police located man missing since July 6\n8",
    "summary": "13 hours ago UPDATED 1:40 p.m. July 8: Cass Keenan has been located and is safe, Eaton Rapids police said. EATON RAPIDS — Police are looking for information about a man who has been missing since early Monday, July 6. Cass Keenan, 31, was last seen about 1 a.m. Monday, Eaton Rapids police said in a Facebook post. When last seen, he was wearing khaki pants and a black short-sleeve shirt, and he was driving a gray Ford F-150 pickup truck with the plate number of B0L04ME.",
